        <h2 id="what">What is the Best Answer Hub Job Keyword Matcher?</h2>
        <p>The Best Answer Hub <a href="/tools/job-keyword-matcher/">Job Keyword Matcher</a> is a single-page tool that compares a job description against your resume and shows a match score, the keywords you already have, and the ones you are missing. You paste the posting and your resume text, and it runs the comparison in your browser with plain JavaScript, so the text is never uploaded, nothing is stored, and it keeps working offline. It needs no account, has no scan limits, and shows no ads. The tool sits in the Best Answer Hub <a href="/career-toolkit/">Career Toolkit</a> and the wider <a href="/tools/">Tools hub</a>, is built and maintained by <a href="/about/shahbaz-ali-malik/">Shahbaz Ali Malik</a>, and stays free because Best Answer Hub is funded by optional paid assessments rather than advertising.</p>

        <div class="cav">The mechanism</div>
        <h2 id="ats">How does an applicant tracking system actually work?</h2>
        <p>An applicant tracking system is a database, not a gatekeeper: it parses your resume into structured fields, stores it as a searchable record, and lets recruiters filter and search by keywords and skills. Workday describes its parsing engine as one that "extracts details from resumes, such as education, skills, and work history" and organizes them into profiles recruiters can search (<a href="https://www.workday.com/en-us/topics/hr/applicant-tracking-system.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Workday</a>). Roughly 98 percent of Fortune 500 companies use one (<a href="https://www.jobscan.co/blog/fortune-500-use-applicant-tracking-systems/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jobscan, 2025</a>). The important part is what it does not do: in most configurations the software does not decide who is rejected. A recruiter searches for the skills a role needs, and a human reviews who comes up. Getting the real terms from the posting onto your resume is what puts you in those search results.</p>
